<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ordinance of Alsnö</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1280</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Alsnö stadga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ordinance of Alsnö was a decree issued around 1280 by King Magnus Ladulås of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> at Alsnö on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-malaren">Lake Mälaren</a>. It freed from taxation those men who served the king as armoured horsemen, creating a privileged class of tax-exempt warriors that became the basis of the Swedish nobility. It also sought to protect peasants from abuses by travelling lords.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ordinance-of-alsno.jpg" alt="Ordinance of Alsnö" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexandru Baboş Albabos · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Magnus_Ladul%C3%A5s_patronus.Riddarholmskyrka_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
